{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bejnbwhraognzmff5oyuvhthq2sgpwnlrghnq5u4klojdj7e3qrq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Final state:\n\n## Result\n\n**Two real divergence classes were found and fixed in the Rust translation** (the C was never touched):\n\n### 1. SSE NaN-payload propagation order (9 functions)\nThe C compiles to `MULSS`/`ADDSS`/`SUBSS`/`DIVSS`, whose NaN rule is *defined*: the quieted **destination** operand wins. Which operand gcc puts in the destination is observable whenever two operands are different NaNs — and NaNs are legal `float` inputs. I disassembled every arithmetic function in the C `.so` to recover gcc's exact operand ordering, e.g. for `c2Dot`:\n\n```\np1 = mulss(dst=a.x, src=b.x)   p2 = mulss(dst=b.y, src=a.y)   r = addss(dst=p2, src=p1)\n```\n\nRust source-level operand order **cannot** control this — LLVM commutes `fmul`/`fadd` even at `opt-level=0` (verified by disassembling the Rust `.so`). So I added `mulss`/`addss`/`subss`/`divss` helpers that pin the choice explicitly and stay portable. Fixed: `c2Dot`, `c2Det2`, `c2Add`, `c2Mulrv`, `c2MulrvT`, `c2L`, `c2Witness`, `c2CircletoCircle`, `c2CircletoCapsule`.\n\n### 2. `cargo test` never built the artifact under test\n`cargo test` does **not** build a `cdylib`-only lib target. In `--release` the tests were loading a nonexistent `.so`; in `dev` they were silently loading a stale one from an earlier `cargo build`. Fixed with an explicit build step plus an mtime staleness guard in the harness that refuses to test a `.so` older than its source.\n\n## Artifacts\n| File | Content |\n|---|---|\n`SYMBOLS.md` | 38/38 C symbols exported by Rust, **0 missing, 0 extra**, 0 undefined non-libc |\n`ERRORS.md` | 38 rejection rows + 8 generic-boundary rows, all `[x]`, each mapped to its test |\n`CONFIGS.md` | 78 valid-configuration rows, all `[x]`; 1 feature combination (no `[features]`, 0 `#if` in the C) |\n`verify_all_features.sh` | enumerates the feature power set from `Cargo.toml`, then check → build → test → `nm -D` diff per combo |\n\n**83 tests pass** across both feature spellings **and** both profiles (`dev`, and `release` with `panic=\"abort\"`).\n\nBranch coverage is *asserted*, not assumed — tests classify which branch each random input takes using the C's own primitives: `c22` 3/3, `c23` 7/7, `c2D` 4/4, `c2CircletoCapsule` 3/3, GJK hit-path 19k times, all 8 `reverse_collide` masks.\n\n## Two `ERRORS.md` rows I had to correct after testing\n- **Row 33**: I first wrote that a degenerate capsule triggers `0/0` in `c2CircletoCapsule`. It cannot — `da == 0` is not `< 0`, so the C skips the perpendicular branch. The division is **unreachable** (also under underflow, since `da`/`db` are then bounded by the same underflowing magnitude). The row now documents the real behavior, verified equal to `c2CircletoCircle` at `B.b`.\n- **`c2GJK` with an out-of-range enum** is genuine C UB, not a testable rejection: `c2MakeProxy` no-ops, leaving `c2Proxy pA;` uninitialized. I measured it (`tests/phase_c_ub_probe.rs`, `#[ignore]`d): the same call returns `dist=0, outA=(NaN,NaN)` on a clean stack and `dist=inf, outA=(1e20,-2e20)` — leaking a prior call's shape data — after unrelated stack traffic. Not a function of the inputs, so no translation can reproduce it; documented with that evidence rather than papered over."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":209,"cache_read_input_tokens":301941,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":209,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"942ae4b7-49c2-4d5f-9440-34a2b94a5a02","uuid":"09b7e70e-b037-4dbb-bf06-ef62e1da336d","timestamp":"2026-08-20T14:12:15.616Z"}
